==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|wërden}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|werdan}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*werþaną}}. Cognate with Dutch {{m|nl|worden}}, Swedish {{m|sv|varda}}, obsolete English verb {{m|en|worth||to become}} and also with Latin {{m|la|vertere||to turn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|De-werden.ogg|audio|lang=de}}
* {{IPA|/ˈveːɐ̯dn̩/|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-irregular|wird|wurde|geworden|past participle 2=worden|auxiliary=sein}}

# {{label|de|auxiliary|with an infinitive|past participle {{m|de|geworden}}}} [[will]]; to be going (to do something); {{non-gloss definition|forms the future tense}}
#: ''Ich '''werde''' nach Hause gehen.''
#:: I '''will''' go home.
# {{label|de|auxiliary|with a past participle|past participle {{m|de|worden}}}} to be done; {{non-gloss definition|forms the passive voice}}
#: ''Das Buch '''wird''' gerade gelesen. (present tense)''
#:: The book is '''being''' read.
#: ''Er war geschlagen '''worden'''. (past perfect tense)''
#:: He had '''been''' beaten.
# {{label|de|intransitive|past participle: “[[geworden]]”}} to [[become]]; to [[get]]; to [[grow]]; to [[turn]]
#: ''Es '''wird''' heißer.''
#:: It's '''getting''' hotter.

